    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing \u2014 the only concrete test class is `AcceptanceTest`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the age-band feature on `POST /api/owners` (surfaced via `GET /api/owners/{id}`). The request may now include an optional ISO `birthDate`, and the response returns an `ageBand` derived against the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (DTOs are generated from this at build time):\n   - Added optional `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema.\n   - Added read-only `ageBand` to the `Owner` response schema as an enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `ageBand(owner)` derivation (mapped into `OwnerDto` via a MapStruct `expression`): null when no `birthDate`; otherwise the full years between `birthDate` and `registrationDate` \u2014 `< 18 \u2192 MINOR`, `18\u201364 \u2192 ADULT`, `\u2265 65 \u2192 SENIOR`. Computed/derived like the other read-only fields rather than persisted. `birthDate` itself maps by name automatically in both directions.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field (`birth_date` column) with getter/setter, so a later GET can recompute `ageBand`.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run against hsqldb; the others were updated for consistency.\n\nThis stayed within the project's conventions: the input DTO comes in at the first step (`BuildOwner`), the entity carries `birthDate` through the pipeline, and `ageBand` is a derived read-only field computed in the mapper at the responder edge \u2014 no new Spring MVC annotations introduced.",
