    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe `ageBand` derivation lands exactly where this codebase already puts derived DTO fields. `OwnerMapper` has an established pattern of small `default` methods \u2014 `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`, `locality`, `contactPreference` \u2014 each taking an `Owner` and computing one `@Mapping` target via `expression = \"java(...)\"`. Adding `ageBand(owner)` alongside `contactPreference(owner)` is purely additive and follows that pattern precisely; it is not duplicated anywhere, and the mapper is the intended home for this kind of derivation rather than a catch-all being stretched.\n\nSupporting changes are proportionate and in the right units: the `birthDate` field + accessors on `Owner` mirror the existing `registrationDate` field exactly, the column is added to all four dialect schemas (consistent coverage), and the OpenAPI additions mark `ageBand` `readOnly` with the enum matching the Java `AgeBandEnum`. Reading the stored `registrationDate` with a `LocalDate.now()` fallback is a reasonable local choice and the Javadoc documents it.\n\nMinor nit (not blocking): the method body uses fully-qualified `java.time.LocalDate`/`java.time.Period` rather than imports \u2014 slightly less tidy than importing \u2014 but the file already uses fully-qualified references elsewhere (`locality`, the `identityKey` expression), so it's in keeping with the file's prevailing style.",
